<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<WorkflowBuilder Version="2.9.0"
                 xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                 xmlns:rx="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Reactive;assembly=Bonsai.Core"
                 xmlns:orc="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Core;assembly=OpenRigs.Core"
                 xmlns:orcl="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Control;assembly=OpenRigs.Control"
                 xmlns:harp="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Harp;assembly=Bonsai.Harp"
                 xmlns:beh="clr-namespace:Harp.Behavior;assembly=Harp.Behavior"
                 xmlns:scr="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions;assembly=Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions"
                 xmlns:io="clr-namespace:Bonsai.IO;assembly=Bonsai.System"
                 xmlns:orl="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Logging;assembly=OpenRigs.Logging"
                 xmlns:lv="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.LiveView;assembly=OpenRigs.LiveView"
                 xmlns="https://bonsai-rx.org/2018/workflow">
  <Description>Calibrates a dome projector's gamma: shows a ramp of grey levels full screen, reads each one's brightness from the Photodiode on the behavior board's ADC0 (AnalogInput0), and writes each level and its reading to calibration\Projector-GammaRamp.csv beside this machine's rig.yml. It measures only: app-rig-control fits the ramp once the run completes and writes the lookup table BonVision's GammaCorrection reads (calibration\Projector-Gamma.bmp, with Projector-Gamma.json recording the ramp and who ran it; the files it replaces go to calibration\_backups\). The board and its clock are the lab's device pieces, each from this machine's rig.yml (ReadLabRig, BehaviorBoard, ClockFromBoard with SetClock false, ReadyGate); a calibration has no experiment folder (OpenRigs.Logging NoExperimentFolder), so no piece logs. The window is OpenRigs.Vision's RawProjectorDisplay: the projector's window with no mesh mapping and no gamma correction, black until a level is drawn on DrawStimuli. DisplayDevice is left at First, as av-dome's window is (app-rig-control passes it to neither); a display the machine lacks stops the workflow at Start. Ready once the board's time is read and the photodiode's first reading arrives; Go runs the ramp; Finished once every level is written.</Description>
  <Workflow>
    <Nodes>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="ConfigRoot" DisplayName="ConfigRoot" Description="The root under which each machine has its own configuration directory, &lt;ConfigRoot&gt;\&lt;RIG&gt;\rig.yml; the ramp is written into calibration\ there." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:ReadLabRig.bonsai">
        <Description>This machine's rig.yml (ConfigRoot\&lt;RIG&gt;\rig.yml) read once into the lab rig model: RigConfigs, RigFile and ConfigRoot, which every device piece reads. First, before anything that reads them.</Description>
        <ConfigRoot>C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs</ConfigRoot>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:NoExperimentFolder.bonsai">
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="SubjectId" />
        <Property Name="SessionId" />
        <Property Name="LaunchId" Description="The launcher's run id; the launch's own, from app-rig-control." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Initialization</Name>
        <Description>The experiment controller (OpenRigs.Control, ExperimentControl) over TCP 5561, which the rig agent relays. Reports Recording at Go.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="SubjectId" />
              <Property Name="SessionId" />
              <Property Name="LaunchId" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Control:ExperimentControl.bonsai">
              <SubjectId />
              <SessionId />
              <LaunchId />
              <ControlEndpoint>@tcp://127.0.0.1:5561</ControlEndpoint>
              <Parameters />
              <Commands />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportPhase">
                <orcl:Phase>Recording</orcl:Phase>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Description>Ends headless Bonsai when it is still running 2 s after the controller's stop: a window or publisher thread held up in teardown (the full-screen projector window, the live view) would keep Bonsai running until the agent's kill; exit code 1 after any other end. Nothing in the editor.</Description>
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:EndAfterStop">
                <orcl:GraceSeconds>2</orcl:GraceSeconds>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="DisplayDevice" DisplayName="DisplayDevice" Description="The display the dome projector is on (OpenRigs.Vision RawProjectorDisplay). First by default, the display the lab's dome windows open on; app-rig-control does not pass it, so a dome whose projector is not Windows' first display needs it in calibrations.toml's [projector.rig] and in that dome's own launch." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Hardware</Name>
        <Description>The lab's device pieces, as in a session (lib-open-rigs building-blocks), never a board opened by hand (Pip, 16 Nov 2026): the Ready gate (ReadyGate), the behavior board BehaviorBoard-Main on rig.yml's port (BehaviorBoard) and its time, read and never set (ClockFromBoard, SetClock false: the board's time, which on a dome follows the timestamp generator; the ramp is timed on Rx timers alone). Its AnalogInput0 (1 kHz, in ADC counts) is published as Photodiode: plug the photodiode facing the screen into the board's ADC0 for the run. Ready once the board's time is read (HarpClockRead) and the first ADC0 reading has arrived (CalibrationReady, this workflow's own stage, ReadyGate's WorkflowStages), so a board sending no analog data stays short of Ready instead of failing at the first level (an empty reading window). The projector's window is here too, as the domes' DomeHardware has it: OpenRigs.Vision RawProjectorDisplay on DisplayDevice, full screen with no mesh mapping and no gamma correction.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:ReadyGate.bonsai">
              <PieceStages>HarpClockRead</PieceStages>
              <WorkflowStages>CalibrationReady</WorkflowStages>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:BehaviorBoard.bonsai">
              <Name>BehaviorBoard-Main</Name>
              <CommandsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</CommandsSubjectName>
              <DataSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Data</DataSubjectName>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:ClockFromBoard.bonsai">
              <Board>BehaviorBoard-Main</Board>
              <SetClock>false</SetClock>
              <BoardDataSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Data</BoardDataSubjectName>
              <BoardCommandsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</BoardCommandsSubjectName>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>BehaviorBoard-Main.Data</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="beh:Parse">
              <harp:Register xsi:type="beh:AnalogData" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>AnalogInput0</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
              <scr:Expression>double(it)</scr:Expression>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:PublishSubject">
              <Name>Photodiode</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Photodiode</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orc:AnnounceStage">
                <orc:Stage>CalibrationReady</orc:Stage>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>ReadyStages</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="DisplayDevice" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Vision:RawProjectorDisplay.bonsai">
              <DisplayDevice>First</DisplayDevice>
              <WindowState>Fullscreen</WindowState>
              <Width>1920</Width>
              <Height>1080</Height>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="12" To="13" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="Levels" DisplayName="Levels" Description="How many grey levels the ramp shows, evenly from black to white; also the lookup table's width. 80 by default, as the lab's lookup tables have." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Calibration</Name>
        <Description>At Go: after 1 s of black, each of Levels grey levels full screen for 0.5 s (fixed: the reading window ends at 0.45 s), its photodiode reading the mean from 0.2 s to 0.45 s in (the level as the level metric). Each level and its reading is written as it comes to calibration\Projector-GammaRamp.csv beside rig.yml, RigFile's folder (columns level, reading; replaced every run). No fit here: once the run completes, app-rig-control interpolates the lookup from the ramp and writes calibration\Projector-Gamma.bmp and Projector-Gamma.json, with backups, refusing a ramp that got no brighter. Reports how many levels were measured as the points metric, then Finished.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>RigFile</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="io:GetDirectoryName" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Format">
              <Format>{0}\calibration\Projector-GammaRamp.csv</Format>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:SelectMany">
              <Name>WriteRamp</Name>
              <Description>The ramp file, opened only once its path is known: a CsvWriter creates its file when the workflow starts, from whatever FileName it has then, and RigFile (an AsyncSubject) arrives a moment later, so a writer mapped from it directly wrote into the workflow's own folder, the lab clone, every run. Started by the path, it writes the rows RampReadings carries.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="FileName" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>RampReadings</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="orl:CsvWriter">
                    <io:FileName>Projector-GammaRamp.csv</io:FileName>
                    <io:Append>false</io:Append>
                    <io:Overwrite>true</io:Overwrite>
                    <io:Suffix>None</io:Suffix>
                    <io:IncludeHeader>true</io:IncludeHeader>
                    <orl:AutoFlush>false</orl:AutoFlush>
                    <orl:PublishRows>false</orl:PublishRows>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="3" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="Levels" DisplayName="Levels" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:SelectMany">
              <Name>Ramp</Name>
              <Description>The levels, one every 0.5 s after 1 s, each drawn full screen and measured; each (level, reading) pair once it is read, also reported as the reading metric ("0.513 412.37": both in one, since app-rig-control polls once a second), completing after the last. The grey level reaches DrawQuad's colour through its own Item1 (workflow_lint shared_mapping_problems): a PropertyMapping fed by a node with other successors is set only after its target has read its properties.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
                    <Property Name="Count" DisplayName="Levels" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="BonVision:Primitives.ParameterRange.bonsai">
                    <Count>80</Count>
                    <RangeMin>0</RangeMin>
                    <RangeMax>1</RangeMax>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Timer">
                      <rx:DueTime>PT1S</rx:DueTime>
                      <rx:Period>PT0.5S</rx:Period>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>Item1</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="ColorR" />
                      <Property Name="ColorG" />
                      <Property Name="ColorB" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>DrawStimuli</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="BonVision:Primitives.DrawQuad.bonsai">
                    <ExtentX>270</ExtentX>
                    <ExtentY>105</ExtentY>
                    <LocationX>0</LocationX>
                    <LocationY>30</LocationY>
                    <Layer>0</Layer>
                    <Angle>0</Angle>
                    <ColorR>0</ColorR>
                    <ColorG>0</ColorG>
                    <ColorB>0</ColorB>
                    <ColorA>1</ColorA>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Format">
                    <Format>{0:0.000}</Format>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                      <orcl:Name>level</orcl:Name>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="rx:SelectMany">
                    <Name>Measure</Name>
                    <Description>The level and the mean Photodiode reading from 0.2 s to 0.45 s after it is shown, once that window closes.</Description>
                    <Workflow>
                      <Nodes>
                        <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                          <Name>Source1</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                          <Name>Photodiode</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Timer">
                            <rx:DueTime>PT0.2S</rx:DueTime>
                            <rx:Period>PT0S</rx:Period>
                          </Combinator>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="rx:SkipUntil" />
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Timer">
                            <rx:DueTime>PT0.45S</rx:DueTime>
                            <rx:Period>PT0S</rx:Period>
                          </Combinator>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="rx:TakeUntil" />
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Average" />
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                      </Nodes>
                      <Edges>
                        <Edge From="1" To="3" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source2" />
                        <Edge From="3" To="5" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source2" />
                        <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="0" To="7" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source2" />
                        <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
                      </Edges>
                    </Workflow>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                  <Expression xsi:type="Format">
                    <Format>{0:0.000} {1:0.00}</Format>
                    <Selector>Item1,Item2</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                      <orcl:Name>reading</orcl:Name>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>Item1</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="2" To="4" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="4" To="15" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="15" To="6" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="6" To="8" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="5" To="9" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="5" To="11" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="11" To="12" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="11" To="13" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="13" To="14" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
              <scr:Expression>new(Item1 as level, Item2 as reading)</scr:Expression>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:PublishSubject">
              <Name>RampReadings</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Count" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Format">
              <Format>{0} levels measured</Format>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                <orcl:Name>points</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportPhase">
                <orcl:Phase>Finished</orcl:Phase>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="4" To="6" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="3" To="9" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="11" To="12" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="lv:StreamDevices">
        <Name>LiveView</Name>
        <Description>Streams every rig.yml device this workflow publishes (its &lt;Device&gt;.Data) to app-rig-control's live view (OpenRigs.LiveView): data on TCP 5556, video on 5558, as in every lab workflow. Last, with nothing feeding it: it finds only subjects built before it.</Description>
        <lv:ConfigRoot>C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs</lv:ConfigRoot>
        <lv:DataPort>5556</lv:DataPort>
        <lv:VideoPort>5558</lv:VideoPort>
      </Expression>
    </Nodes>
    <Edges>
      <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
    </Edges>
  </Workflow>
</WorkflowBuilder>
